{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST tell agents that drafts may be high-level, compound, or incomplete, and that they need not answer every question before review.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations. The `habeas-requirements` skill must tell agents that drafts may be high-level, compound, or incomplete. It must also tell them that they need not answer every question before review.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_allows_rough_drafts_before_review]` carries the `{test}` reference. It finds the skill's \"Write drafts\" step with `step_of` and `step`. `assert_text` then asserts that this step contains two phrases:\n- \"Drafts may be high-level, compound, or incomplete\". This covers the first obligation, using the requirement's own wording.\n- \"Ask the user only what the request can't answer; the review in step 3 finds the rest\". This covers the second obligation, because it tells agents not to resolve every question before review and to leave the rest to the review.\n\nThe helpers behave as needed. `assert_text` asserts `contains` for each phrase and fails with a label if one is missing. `step_of` panics if no step contains the \"Write drafts\" heading. `step` panics if the step is missing, so the assertions run against the right step.\n\nThe requirement is a single content statement with no boundaries or modes. The test covers both clauses, so I found no gap.",
